## Operating-logic semantics (item 7)
REQ-S07-007 DG4 | Compute RAG from the approved expected trajectory with configurable thresholds and never from project task completion 
   A: A04;A05: with all tasks complete and actual below the red threshold the KPI is Red; changing the threshold version recomputes RAG
REQ-PB-063 DG4 | Apply the area-specific T10 RAG logic 
   A: A04;A05: an outcome whose tasks are 100% complete but KPI is below trajectory is Red/Amber, not Green; a KPI with no actual shows Unknown
REQ-S03-003 DG4 | Keep initiative delivery, business adoption, validated value and transformation closure as separate statuses 
   A: A11: setting delivery to Complete leaves adoption, validated value and closure unchanged; the API rejects a closure request while validated value is pending unless a transition decision exists
REQ-S11-006 DG4 | Show delivery complete, value validation pending and BAU accepted as separate states so success is never inferred from initiative completion 
   A: A11: with all initiatives complete and value pending, the transformation shows 'Delivery complete - value validation pending', not successful
REQ-S08-001 DG4 | Track planned, forecast, measured, submitted-for-validation, validated, rejected and sustained benefit values separately 
   A: A10: a forecast amount never appears in the validated total; a rejected measurement is retained and shown as rejected
REQ-S08-016 DG4 | Keep measure-only submissions out of the validated total until approved 
   A: A10: submitting a measurement leaves the validated total unchanged; approval increases it by exactly the approved amount
REQ-PB-013 DG4 | Restrict Finance / Value Office validation of baseline, benefit logic and value realization to the Finance role 
   A: A10;A12: a Business Owner calling the validate endpoint receives 403; a Finance user succeeds and the audit event records validator identity
REQ-S08-003 DG4 | Record for each benefit a unique ID, type, accountable business owner, Finance validator where applicable, baseline/counterfactual, formula, driver units, targe 
   A: A10: a financial benefit without a financial-statement mapping, or a non-financial one without an agreed KPI, is rejected
REQ-PB-058 DG4 | Prevent double counting: each benefit has a unique owner, baseline, formula and financial-statement or non-financial KPI link 
   A: A10: a benefit with two owners is rejected; a 10 million SAR benefit shared by two initiatives appears once (10 million SAR) in the portfolio total
REQ-S08-013 DG4 | Reject allocations over 100% and show any share below 100% as unallocated 
   A: A10: allocations 60% + 50% are rejected; 60% + 30% saves and shows 10% unallocated
REQ-S04-002 DG4 | Make gates explicit approval records tied to a versioned, immutable evidence snapshot, never inferred from task completion 
   A: A07;A08: completing every phase task leaves the gate Draft; editing a record after submission does not change the snapshot content shown to approvers
REQ-PB-015 DG4 | Model the six stage gates G1-G6 as explicit approval records with decision question and evidence required 
   A: A08: submission with missing mandatory evidence is rejected; approval by a non-approver returns 403; approval of a stale submission version is rejected
REQ-DLV-002 DG0 | Keep engineering delivery gates DG0-DG7 separate from product business approvals G1-G6 in records, authority and meaning 
   A: A23;A28: gate records validate only with stage_id DG0-DG7; CLAUDE.md and agent-protocol.md state that G6 never implies DG7 and that no agent grants a business, Finance or IT approval
REQ-PB-001 DG5 | Label the methodology provenance honestly as a practical synthesis inspired by PMI/Brightline/BRM and never claim official PMI status 
   A: A01: provenance text on reader/About/report footer matches B0004 verbatim; an automated text scan of UI strings (en+ar) and report templates finds no claim of 'official PMI standard', 'PMI certified' or equivalent
REQ-S15-002 DG1 | Seed the provisional design tokens brand.primary #0078FF, brand.deep #003B73, surface.page #F5F8FC, surface.card #FFFFFF, text.primary #142438, text.secondary # 
   A: A20: the API returns the seven tokens with the values listed and provenance=provisional; no UI string or document claims official Mobily brand compliance

